## DUNE VNC 2026

[https://wiki.dunescience.org/wiki/DUNE\_Computing/Using\_VNC\_Connections\_on\_the\_dunegpvms](https://wiki.dunescience.org/wiki/DUNE_Computing/Using_VNC_Connections_on_the_dunegpvms)   
As suggested for dunegpvm setup in the document above: .vnc, .config/tigervnc/, and vncpasswd tasks were completed \- here I am running on MacOS Sequoia 15.7.5

mac$ kinit [demuth@FNAL.GOV](mailto:demuth@FNAL.GOV)   
mac$ ssh demuth@dunegpvm13fnal.gov  
\<dunegpvm13.fnal.gov\> source /nashome/d/dbrailsf/setupVNC.sh  
This generates an excerpt for the laptop’s .ssh/config making some basic changes in Host and HostName line, noting the line with localhost:11564 is created  
\#------------------------------------------  
Host dunegpvm??  
  HostName %h.fnal.gov  
  User demuth  
  ForwardAgent yes  
  ForwardX11 yes  
  ForwardX11Trusted yes  
  GSSAPIAuthentication yes  
  GSSAPIDelegateCredentials yes  
  LocalForward 5901 localhost:11564  
\#------------------------------------------  
\<dunegpvm13.fnal.gov\> exit  
mac$ emacs \-nw \~/.ssh/config-dunegpvmXX ← creating a dunegpvmXX specific config  
Make any additions, then launch ssh from mac$ using config-dunegpvmXX  
mac$ ssh \-F \~/.ssh/config-dunegpvmXX dunegpvm13  
\<dunegpvm13.fnal.gov\> source /nashome/d/dbrailsf/setupVNC.sh  
Inspect for localhost number, here 11564 \- okay, no changes  
\<dunegpvm13.fnal.gov\> vncpasswd  
Enter an 8 character pw and repeat enter, no to view-only pw

On mac, open 🍎\>System Settings, Remote Management, set On, Anyone may request permission to control screen On, VNC viewers may control screen with password On, Always show Remote Management status in menu bar On. Here also, you want to set the Password to the one you set on the dunegpvm via the vncpasswd. Screen Sharing was first turned on but control was delegated to Remote Management that was updated.  
![][image1]  
Verify port  
mac$ lsof \-i :5901  
mac$ open vnc://localhost:5901

![][image2]

Enter vncpasswd here, then verify port again  
mac$ lsof \-i :5901  
![][image3]

